WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.667
-Jeff Gordon, I always love seeing you, bud.

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.767
-I love seeing you. It's been too long, though.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:06.334
-It's been too -- -Why has it been so long?

00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:08.067
-I know. I want you to come on more than once a year, yeah.

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:10.100
-I love hanging out with you. We have good times.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.934
-I mean, this is crazy. 75 years of NASCAR.

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:14.667
-Yes. -That's wild.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:17.501
-What's really wild is I remember 50.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:19.968
You know, I won the championship back in --

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:22.267
I think it was in '98, when they celebrated their 50th

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.601
and won the championship that year.

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:26.567
And here we are 25 years later doing 75.

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:29.701
-I have a photo of you from 1992.

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:30.901
Atlanta Motor Speedway.

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:32.434
-Oh, I don't know if I want to see that.

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:33.734
-Well, you got to look at the m--

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:35.300
Look at this mustache. I mean, look at that.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.234
Look at that. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:40.400
That's -- That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.968
-Hey, if you wanted to be a NASCAR driver in the '90s,

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:45.701
that's the way you had to look.

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:47.033
[ Laughter ] -Really?

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:48.767
-No. -No. No.

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:51.767
But I heard there's a little strategy to this mustache.

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:53.400
-Well, you have to understand.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.868
I started racing at a very young age.

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:57.601
I think I was growing a mustache at, like, 12 years old

00:00:57.601 --> 00:01:00.400
for the first time, and I was racing against

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.901
all these older guys, and I wanted to feel like I fit in

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:05.400
and, you know, look older.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.634
It didn't make -- It didn't work, but I tried.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:10.067
-No, you look like an actual baby here with a mustache.

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:11.567
-But you have to understand.

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:14.501
Richard Petty, Dale Earnhardt, Dale Jarrett.

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.601
I mean, all the greats had mustaches,

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:18.934
so I thought I needed one. -Yeah.

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:21.367
-Luckily it didn't last but another year.

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:23.167
-Do you remember your first race?

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:27.367
-Um, absolutely because, one, it was memorable

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:30.667
because I backed into the wall at about lap 50.

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:32.267
-Geez.

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:33.467
-But it was Richard Petty's final race.

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:35.267
You know, how many people can say

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:37.133
they got to race against The King?

00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:39.701
-But this is -- You brought me, actually --

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:41.000
-Yes, we did. -Look at this.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.100
-Well, we've got to celebrate 75 years of NASCAR.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.968
-Look at that. I love this right here.

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:45.968
And you signed it for me, too.

00:01:45.968 --> 00:01:47.834
-Well, I mean, you know, we're --

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:50.100
[ Cheers and applause ] Absolutely.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.734
-Do you ever get tempted to get behind the wheel and go,

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:55.133
"I'm gonna show these guys how it's done"?

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:57.067
-No. I mean, I -- I know how hard it is

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:59.133
to get back in there and compete at that level.

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:00.868
But I still love to drive fast.

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:03.367
I mean, I get in a -- I actually did a race,

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.334
a sports-car race this last year,

00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:07.300
and it did remind me how hard you have to work

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.968
'cause I got beat pretty bad, but -- but I love it.

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:11.667
I just love getting in the car,

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:14.667
and just the fun of it is what got me into racing.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:17.667
And I just don't want to do the high-level competition.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:20.234
-How are you in the car, like, going to the mall or something?

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:21.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:24.033
-I feel like I'm an excellent driver.

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:26.367
I mean, I've got to say -- you know, I don't have any --

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:28.367
-Are you -- Are you left-lane guy all the way?

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:30.501
-I'm left lane if I'm passing.

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:32.567
I mean, you don't belong in the left lane

00:02:32.567 --> 00:02:34.701
unless you're doing something. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:38.000
-Wow! That's getting a standing ovation right now.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.501
Thank you for saying that.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:40.767
-Yes. -Yes.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:42.501
-I mean, I don't always hang in the left lane.

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:45.234
If I'm not in a hurry, I'll go in the middle lane,

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:46.734
I'll go in the right lane. -Yeah, yeah.

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:48.734
Alright, alright, good. 75th --

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.534
-But let's be honest. I'm more in the left lane.

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:51.801
-You're left lane. Yeah, alright.

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:53.834
I figured. Alright, good. You don't lie to me, yeah.

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:55.367
What do we have to expect this season --

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:57.200
February, 75 years of NASCAR?

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.901
-What I love about this year is there's several events

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:01.534
that are going to be happening

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:04.067
that I think are going to really sum up 75 years.

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:06.434
Because, first of all, we kick off the season

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:07.734
in a stadium.

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:10.901
L.A. Coliseum is where we start this season off.

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:12.767
We did it last year, but we're going to do it again.

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:15.133
And it's just amazing to see the entertainment

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:18.200
and the racing that close up in this tiny arena.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.767
-Yeah. -And then we're going to go to

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:22.067
a street-course race for the first time in history of NASCAR.

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:23.434
-Talk to me about that. -Chicago.

00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:26.334
Yeah, downtown Chicago. Right on the streets.

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:28.968
I mean, they're going to set up a street course.

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:30.501
We've seen other forms of motorsports do it,

00:03:30.501 --> 00:03:33.534
but never big, heavy stock cars, loud, roaring stock cars.

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:34.701
-Yeah!

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.367
-It's going to be pretty amazing.

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:38.934
I can't wait to see how that turns out.

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:40.267
Plus, it's going to be a festival.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.267
There's going to be music and parties.

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:43.467
So it should be really cool.

00:03:43.467 --> 00:03:45.467
And then we're going to do a throwback,

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:47.567
where we're going to go back to North Wilkesboro,

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:49.501
which has not -- I don't think there's been a race there

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:51.901
in, like, 25 or 30 years.

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:54.367
So it's incredible that we're, you know, going to --

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.534
And we've got such young talent that's out there.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:58.400
So it's exciting. -What do you tell

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.767
the young talent when they ask you for advice?

00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:01.968
Do you go like, "Ugh.

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:03.200
First of all, let me show you how to do it"?

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.634
Or do you just -- -No.

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:07.534
No, you know, these guys are in the car every weekend.

00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:09.367
I mean, they know what they need.

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:13.300
To me, it's all about, you know, trying to help them

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:16.534
have the guidance or the resources

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:18.033
or just connecting people, you know?

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:20.734
It's a people business. It's all about teamwork.

00:04:20.734 --> 00:04:22.400
It's all about the people you work with

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.367
and making sure that they have confidence in you

00:04:24.367 --> 00:04:26.167
and you have confidence in them.

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:28.167
Of course, there's the branding, the marketing.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.133
I think I could probably work more with them

00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:32.734
on that side of it, of the experience that I've had

00:04:32.734 --> 00:04:35.701
over the years, more so than I could probably do

00:04:35.701 --> 00:04:37.200
anything for them on the track.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.801
You know, I've not been in a car in seven, eight years.

00:04:39.801 --> 00:04:41.601
-But, still, you're Jeff Gordon.

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:43.167
Come on, buddy. Like, come on, yeah.

00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:45.467
-I mean, if we go to Martinsville, now, maybe.

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:48.133
-Yeah! That's what I'm talking about! Yeah!

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:49.868
You're one of the best ever to do it, bud.

00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:51.734
Always good to see you. You know I love you, bud.

00:04:51.734 --> 00:04:53.200
Jeff Gordon. -Thank you.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.501
-Check out the 75th anniversary season

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:57.267
of NASCAR beginning February 5th.

00:04:57.267 --> 00:04:59.267
We'll be right back with Lauren London.

00:04:59.267 --> 00:05:00.634
Stick around, everybody.

